# 9/11/2026 -- hacker waves 3/4: NBBO-priced Simple/Activetaker replaces the Seeker rest

## What changed
- hacker_trades.py: the wave-3 Seeker rest (surface-quoting, limit forced to -HACK_MAX_PRICE
  via WAVE3_FORCE_CLAMP_EDGE=99) is replaced by two NBBO-priced waves:
    WAVE 3: remainder sent Simple/Activetaker at limit = -(live cross + HACK_W3_NBBO_OFFSET
      0.07), floored at -HACK_MAX_PRICE (1.70). Works HACK_W3_WORK_S = 10s, then the
      status-gated batched_fill_check_and_cancel settles it.
    WAVE 4: any W3 remainder re-priced off a REFRESHED NBBO at -(cross + HACK_W4_NBBO_OFFSET
      0.15), same floor, resting orderDuration = seconds to 16:00:00 (self-expires; capped by
      WAVE_REST_MAX_DURATION_S = 310 for test-harness runs).
  NBBO source (_nbbo_table): v7 sranalytics.msgoptionimpliedquote; v8
  sranalytics.msgliveimpliedquote (the F4 table, NOT the adj proxy). Refresh retries 3x, 1s
  apart, on failure/missing leg/ask<=0/row older than 5s; after that it SENDS ANYWAY on the
  freshest quote held (fire-time leg rows as last resort) -- per Zach: never a silent
  no-order, and never a bare -1.70 limit (LmtCollar reject risk; cap can only bind when the
  cross is already near it).
- spdr_rock_order_functions.py: trade_complex/_send_single_complex_order gained
  limit_class="Surface", parent_handling="Seeker", explicit_limit=None kwargs -- defaults
  byte-identical for every existing caller; the hacker passes Simple/Activetaker + the
  NBBO-derived limit. WAVE3_FORCE_CLAMP_EDGE deleted.
- Exception isolation preserved: W3/W4 sit in the existing never-lose-wave-1/2-codes guard,
  W4 nested so its failure cannot lose W3's code. Announced sleep ("sleeping 10s for WAVE-3
  to work") keeps the daily review's gap classifier clean.

## Why
The old wave 3 was believed to be a plain working limit at 1.70 (chat "Hacker script max
spread price", and the hacker backtest models fill-at-cross up to the cap), but as coded it
was a Seeker quoting at surface+ET2 with 1.70 only as an outer bound -- more passive than the
validated model exactly on fast-market days. 9/9 evidence: wave-3 fills at 1.00-1.10 vs
quotes it could have crossed; the model/prod gap surfaced as "attempted but never filled,
delta_pnl 0" lines.

